AB  - In an industrial sugar making process, the extracted raw juice out of the sugarcane is first clarified in the sugar refineries, and then its crystallization is carried out in vacuum pans. In the sugar refineries, the pH control is performed in three steps viz. liming, carbonation, and sulphitation. The pH control unit for the sugar mill is the area of research chosen to write this research paper. In this work, for a considered transfer function model of the pH control system, the controller is designed in MATLAB using two different approaches viz. the robust control based on the H infinity loop shaping technique and the digital control using MPC (model predictive control) technique. The set-point response of both control systems have been analyzed and compared. © 2022 IEEE
